    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## \ud83c\udfac IMDB Sentiment \u2014 what happened to our model?\n**1. The A1 model** (TF-IDF + Logistic Regression) was trained on **dataset v1**: 50K long IMDB reviews, 50% positive.\n**2. The data drifted \u2192 dataset v2**: reviews got ~75% shorter, new slang showed up (*mid, fire, goated*), and 70% of reviews became negative.\n**3. The A1 model struggled** on the new reviews (see the red drop below), because it had never seen the new words.\n**4. We retrained \u2192 model v2** on dataset v2 (with balanced class weights). It recovers on the drifted reviews.\n*Everything here is read live from MLflow's database (runs, metrics, model registry).*"
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-postgresql-datasource",
        "uid": "mlflow-db"
      }
    },
    {
